          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Unnamed first-person narrator\",\"addressee\":\"Maria\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i\\nNød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig. Javel har jeg længtes efter\\nmin yndige Elskerindes Kærtegn. Men mest har jeg længtes efter alt\\ndet andet, som ogsaa er Dig: dit trofaste Hjærte, din rene Tanke,\\ndin milde Tale, dit lyse Smil, som er min Sol i Tvivlen, dit gode\\nHaandtryk, som er min Styrke paa Vejen.\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly and emphatically avows the narrator's present loving state in response to Maria's concern that his apparent change may be temporary or imagined.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The exact focal expression asserts love but does not itself specify an undertaking, obligation, or promised course of action. Commitments articulated in the following sentences must not be transferred onto this marked occurrence.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil\\njeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"Although spoken during an emotional reunion, the expression is a deliberate, syntactically framed answer to Maria's question rather than a reflex-like affective discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg svarer: »Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt\\nend for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"The focal expression's core force is adequately represented as a truth-conditional avowal of love; the supplied evidence does not establish a distinct residual function beyond T.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"elsker jeg Dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"At their reunion, Maria asks whether the narrator's apparent love is genuine, enduring, and not merely a temporary product of longing. He answers her directly with the focal avowal, framed as an emphatic assurance.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal words themselves undertake no specific action. The surrounding turn separately presents enduring companionship and living together, but those commitments are not part of the exact target. Maria's crying from happiness and her represented understanding that he speaks truth show that she receives the larger answer as sincere reassurance; the scene does not separately record formal acceptance of any undertaking within the focal words.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognise the work from the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage strongly represents the avowal as sincere, but literary narration cannot independently verify the speaker's internal state. The exact target is only a short clause, so commitment language in neighbouring sentences has been treated as context rather than as part of its force.\"}"
